info.description:
API for the "Трамплин" career platform

Refined MVP contract between backend and frontend for the "Трамплин" platform.

This revision aligns the API with `Tramplin.dbml` and the original technical specification.
It keeps the role model, moderation flow, notifications, and location-aware public catalog,
while correcting enum values and DTO shapes that had drifted from the data model.

Key alignment points:
  - database-backed enum values are used consistently;
  - public company responses exclude verification-only fields;
  - saved entities and employer application flows expose stored metadata;
  - media metadata matches the `media_files` table, while access is derived from the entity a file is attached to.

Authentication is implemented with stateless JWT tokens transported in HttpOnly cookies.
Protected browser requests must be sent with credentials included.

Curator administration invariant:
  - exactly one platform administrator exists at any time;
  - the administrator is also a curator and has all ordinary curator permissions;
  - only that administrator can create and manage other curator accounts;
  - creating a second administrator through public API is not supported.

Generated from TramplinAPI.yaml.

Auth is cookie-based. Login once in Postman and reuse the same environment/session so cookies persist.

For local manual testing, import the bundled `Tramplin Local` environment and run `make infra-start`, `make db-migrate`, `make seed-dev`, then `make run`.

request.description:
Business constraints:
  - only applicant users can apply;
  - only one application may ever exist per applicant/opportunity pair;
  - target opportunity must be publicly available for applying;
  - applicant cannot apply to closed, rejected, archived, or expired opportunity;
  - application is created with status=submitted.

operationId: `createApplication`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - only the owning applicant can withdraw the application;
  - allowed from statuses: submitted, reviewing, reserve;
  - not allowed from accepted, rejected, withdrawn.

operationId: `withdrawMyApplication`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - only applicant users can create connections;
  - self-connection is forbidden;
  - there can be only one connection record for an unordered pair of applicants.

operationId: `createConnection`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - only participants of the connection can update it;
  - accepted/rejected/blocked are terminal outcomes for the pending request;
  - blocked may later be handled by a dedicated unblock flow if introduced.

operationId: `patchConnection`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Returns applicant profile filtered by applicant privacy settings.
Visibility rules:
  - private -> owner and curators only;
  - contacts_only -> accepted contacts, owner, and curators;
  - employers_only -> employer users, owner, and curators;
  - authenticated_public -> any authenticated user and curators.
Curators may always read the profile for moderation purposes.
The returned payload does not expose the applicant's raw privacy settings.

operationId: `getApplicantProfileById`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - target employer is resolved by employerEmail and must already have an employer account;
  - any approved member may create a new pending membership or reopen a rejected/revoked membership;
  - pending or approved membership for the same employer/company pair cannot be duplicated;
  - only owners may invite directly into memberRole=owner or request isPrimaryContact=true;
  - managers may invite only recruiter/hr/manager memberships.

operationId: `createCompanyMembership`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - target membership must belong to the specified company;
  - only approved memberships may be edited through this endpoint;
  - only owners may assign or remove memberRole=owner;
  - managers may change only non-owner memberships and may assign only recruiter/hr/manager roles;
  - only owners may set isPrimaryContact=true; setting it reassigns primary contact to the target membership.

operationId: `patchCompanyMembership`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - target membership must belong to the specified company and be pending;
  - owners may approve any pending membership;
  - managers may approve only non-owner memberships.

operationId: `approveCompanyMembership`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - target membership must belong to the specified company and be pending;
  - owners may reject any pending membership;
  - managers may reject only non-owner memberships;
  - comment is required for auditability.

operationId: `rejectCompanyMembership`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - target membership must belong to the specified company and be approved;
  - owners may revoke any approved membership, except the last approved owner membership;
  - managers may revoke only non-owner memberships;
  - comment is required for auditability.

operationId: `revokeCompanyMembership`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - only approved company members can submit verification requests;
  - a company may have at most one active request in pending/under_review state;
  - evidence requirements depend on verification method.

operationId: `createCompanyVerificationRequest`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Business constraints:
  - current employer must have approved membership in the target company;
  - newly created opportunity starts in status=draft;
  - moderation_status is initialized according to moderation workflow, usually pending;
  - detail block must match `type`:
      vacancy/internship -> vacancyDetails required;
      mentor_program -> mentorProgramDetails required;
      event -> eventDetails required.

operationId: `createOpportunity`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Updates editable content of an employer opportunity.
Business constraints for status transitions:
  - draft -> planned, archived;
  - planned -> active, archived;
  - active -> closed, archived;
  - closed -> archived;
  - rejected -> draft, archived;
  - archived is terminal.

Additional constraints:
  - rejected is normally set by moderation workflow, not ordinary employer editing;
  - active/planned opportunities intended for public catalog must have moderation_status=approved;
  - changing type after creation is not supported in MVP;
  - once moderation_status=approved, content fields are immutable in MVP;
    only lifecycle actions such as activate/close/archive remain available.

operationId: `patchEmployerOpportunity`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Allowed status transitions:
  - submitted -> reviewing, reserve, rejected;
  - reviewing -> reserve, accepted, rejected;
  - reserve -> reviewing, accepted, rejected;
  - accepted, rejected, withdrawn are terminal.

Additional constraints:
  - withdrawn can only be set by applicant withdrawal endpoint;
  - status changes append a record to application_status_history;
  - comment is optional but recommended for rejected/reserve decisions.

operationId: `patchApplicationStatus`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Audience constraints:
  - single_applicant -> exactly one applicantUserId;
  - selected_applicants -> one or more applicantUserIds;
  - all_applicants_of_opportunity -> opportunityId required, applicantUserIds omitted.

operationId: `createNotificationCampaign`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Review result semantics:
  - approved -> company becomes verified;
  - rejected -> request closed as rejected;
  - needs_changes -> request returned to employer;
  - under_review -> request stays open and assigned.

A non-empty reviewComment is required for rejected and needs_changes reviews, and optional for approved or under_review.

operationId: `reviewVerificationRequest`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.

Moderation state semantics:
  - pending -> newly created or not yet acted upon;
  - approved -> target content accepted;
  - rejected -> target content rejected;
  - needs_changes -> target should be fixed and resubmitted.

Every moderation case update must include a non-empty reason for auditability.

operationId: `patchModerationCase`

Auth: cookie-based session. Use `/auth/login` first; Postman should retain the auth cookies automatically.
